  "goodToKnow": "Schwelgen means to indulge or revel: in Erinnerungen schwelgen (to reminisce fondly), in Luxus schwelgen, in Farben schwelgen (of a painting). Originally it meant to feast lavishly. Synonyms: genießen, sich ergötzen, frönen. Don't confuse it with schwellen (to swell) or schweigen (to be silent). Regular: schwelgte, geschwelgt."
